-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------IOS-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
Cisco IOS shell prompt modes:
CONFIG MODES		|PROMPT		|ALLOWENCE			|CMD TO USE MODE
1. User-EXEC		|>		|-				|end (brings 1 level down => use multiple times untill desired level reached)
2. Privileged-EXEC	|#		|viewing & debugging configs	|enable
3. Global-Config	|(config)#	|all				|configure terminal



-----------------------------------------------LAB----------------------------------------------------
Show Running Configuration
	R1#show running-config [brief] [| section <section>]	// use pipes (|) for filtering

Show Interface details
	R1#show interface [<intNo> | brief]			// interfaces's all details
	R1#show ip interface [<intNo> | brief]			// interface's ip details

Set Speed of Ethernet Interface
	R1(config-if)#speed <megabits/s>			// affects physical speed of ethernet interface

Set Clock-Rate of Serial Interface
	R1(config-if)#clock rate <kilobits/s>			// affects physical clock-rate of serial interface

Set Interface Bandwidth
	R1(config-if)#bandwidth <megabits/s>			// affects software policies NOT physical speed

Set Interface MTU
	R1(config-if)#mtu <bytes>				// default: 1500 bytes; affects all packets out of interface

Set Interface IP MTU
	R1(config-if)#ip mtu <bytes>				// default: 1500 bytes; affects only ip packets out of interface

Turn off all debugs
	R1#undebug all						// turn off all debugs

Select Range of Interfaces
	SW1(config)#interface range FastEthernet 0/3 - 5	// selectes all interfaces from FE 0/3 through 0/5